course: dictionary
lesson: 1099
title: Brainstorm and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Brainstorm is a word you will hear a lot at school. Read the words around it to work out what it means. «Teachers often allow AI for brainstorming but not for writing your work.» The sentence says brainstorming is allowed, but the writing itself must be your own. So brainstorming must be the part before the writing, where you gather ideas.
explain: Ask: what word would fit here? Try a meaning in the sentence. Replace brainstorming with "thinking of lots of ideas" and it still makes sense: teachers allow AI for thinking of lots of ideas, but not for writing your work. That is a good check.
explain: The sentence also gives a warning: «ask first when unsure». When you do not know whether a tool or task is allowed, the clue tells you to check with your teacher.
fact: Brainstorm (verb) means to think of lots of ideas quickly, writing them all down before choosing the best.
fact: A brainstorm (noun) is a session of doing this, often in a group.
fact: In school, children brainstorm ideas in a mind map or spider diagram before they write a story.
fact: Teams brainstorm solutions in work and science projects.
fact: Brainstorm ideas is a common phrase, and it means thinking up lots of ideas first.
exercise: What does brainstorm mean in «Teachers often allow AI for brainstorming but not for writing your work»? | Sleeping on a problem | Writing the final story neatly | *Thinking of lots of ideas before writing | Finishing your homework quickly
exercise: In a science project, a team needs to solve a problem. What might they do first? | Stop thinking and go home | *Brainstorm solutions together | Play a game | Hide their ideas from each other
exercise: What does brainstorm mean as a verb? | *To think of lots of ideas quickly | To write very neatly | To paint a picture slowly | To sleep for a long time
test: Before writing a story, what do children often do in a mind map or spider diagram? | *Brainstorm ideas | Draw a picture only | Sleep | Copy a book
test: The sentence says «ask first when unsure». What should you do if you are not sure a tool is allowed? | *Ask your teacher first | Use it anyway | Hide it from everyone
exam: Which phrase in «Teachers often allow AI for brainstorming but not for writing your work» shows the writing must be your own? | Teachers often | *not for writing your work | brainstorming | allow AI
